sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant RHODS as rhods-operator
    participant API as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant AIHub as aihub-controller-manager
    participant CatOp as catalog-controller-manager<br/>webhook 9443/TCP
    participant MROp as model-registry-operator<br/>webhook 9443/TCP
    participant User as User / Dashboard / SDK
    participant GW as data-science-gateway<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Proxy as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS (service-ca)
    participant REST as rest-container<br/>127.0.0.1:8080 HTTP
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / MySQL<br/>5432 / 3306
    participant Img as registry.redhat.io<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over RHODS,CatOp: Flow 1 - Module installation
    RHODS->>API: Apply overlays/aihub, create AIHub default-aihub<br/>rhods-operator SA
    API-->>AIHub: Watch AIHub
    AIHub->>API: Create instances namespace (rhoai-model-registries)
    AIHub->>API: SSA odh bundle: CRDs, webhooks, RBAC,<br/>2 operator Deployments, NetworkPolicies, Templates
    AIHub->>API: Poll child Deployment availability,<br/>then create Catalog "catalog"
    API->>CatOp: Validate Catalog (443→9443 TLS service-ca)
    CatOp-->>API: Allowed
    AIHub->>API: Update AIHub status (ModelRegistryReady,<br/>CatalogReady, CatalogDataReady)
    API-->>RHODS: DSC AIHubReady

    Note over User,DB: Flow 2 - ModelRegistry provisioning
    User->>API: Create ModelRegistry (user token + RBAC)
    API->>MROp: Mutate + validate (443→9443 TLS)
    MROp-->>API: Defaulted / allowed
    MROp->>API: Create Deployment, Service, SA, Role, Group,<br/>CRB, NetworkPolicies, Route, HTTPRoute, ReferenceGrant
    REST->>DB: Connect (DB password, TLS optional, default off)

    Note over User,REST: Flow 3 - Client access via Gateway
    User->>GW: HTTPS /model-registry/{name}/<br/>Bearer token
    GW->>Proxy: Rewrite to /, HTTPS 8443 (TLS service-ca)<br/>Bearer forwarded
    Proxy->>API: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview<br/>(get services/{name}, auth-delegator)
    API-->>Proxy: Allowed
    Proxy->>REST: HTTP 8080 (loopback, no auth)
    REST-->>Proxy: Response
    Proxy-->>GW: Response
    GW-->>User: JSON response

    Note over CatOp,Img: Flow 4 - Catalog data image update
    CatOp->>API: Manage ImageStreams model-catalog-data,<br/>model-catalog-benchmark-data (scheduled import)
    API->>Img: OpenShift image controller imports<br/>ai-hub-catalog-rhel9:stable (cluster pull secret)
    CatOp->>API: Roll out model-catalog (init copy + validate data,<br/>record activation hash in status)
